# nr-office-pdf-preview: mixdog_office_pdf::preview (documentPreviewPdf and documentPreviewPages of pdf/document-preview.mjs)

Not compiled: cargo was not run (the lead compiles the wave). The module is not part of the crate until the lines below are applied.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office-pdf/src/lib.rs

After `pub mod render;` add:

    pub mod preview;

(The doc comment at the top of lib.rs may name `pdf/document-preview.mjs` among the ported files. The module is used by its path,
`mixdog_office_pdf::preview::{DocumentPreview, SystemEngines, RasterPages, ...}`: no `pub use` is needed.)

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office-pdf/Cargo.toml

[dependencies], keeping the list sorted, add (all are workspace dependencies already locked; only new edges of mixdog-office-pdf, no cycle:
mixdog-office-com depends on fsio, rt, regex, serde_json, sha2, tokio, tokio-util, zip; mixdog-office-crypto on aes, base64, md-5, fsio,
quick-xml, sha1, sha2):

    mixdog-office-com = { workspace = true }
    mixdog-office-crypto = { workspace = true }
    sha2 = { workspace = true }

and change the tokio line to add the feature `sync` (the shared conversion of two opens of one document is a `tokio::sync::OnceCell`; the
tests use `tokio::sync::oneshot`):

    tokio = { workspace = true, features = ["rt", "sync", "time", "process", "io-util"] }

[dev-dependencies]: the tests build a multi-thread runtime (a password derivation blocks the thread of its lane job, so the cancellation
test needs a second thread):

    tokio = { workspace = true, features = ["rt", "rt-multi-thread"] }

The tests need no other dependency (sha2, base64, mixdog-fsio, mixdog-office-crypto, mixdog-rt and mixdog-testkit are listed already or above).
`mixdog-rt` in [dev-dependencies] already has `test-support` (the tests take their lanes from `mixdog_rt::testing::tokens()`).

## native/core/Cargo.lock

Package mixdog-office-pdf: add `mixdog-office-com`, `mixdog-office-crypto`, `sha2` to its dependencies. No new package (`cargo update -w` offline writes it).

## native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml

Run the repository's hakari check after the edges above; take its output if it asks for a feature of tokio.

