The recording was made from a scratch checkout whose git history is not the product's (the recorder was run with `--tree C:/Project/mixdog` and the
recorders' lib copied beside it), so the manifest's `product.commit` is null and `refComparison.closestCommit` names that scratch commit. Re-record once from
the integration checkout (`node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-preview.mjs --tree <Node product tree>`): the documents carry the random salts of
their encryption, so golden.json changes; re-run `twin_preview` against it and update the digest above.

## What the callers must do (interfaces added)

- `mixdog_office_pdf::preview::DocumentPreview::new(lanes, engines, renderer)` is the preview of a process (clones share the caches). The engines of a
  process are `SystemEngines::new(lanes, office_com)` (LibreOffice through `mixdog_ooxml::soffice::Soffice::process()`, Microsoft Office through
  `mixdog_office_com::OfficeCom`) and `RasterPages::new(lanes, font_registry, write_note)` (`render_pdf_pages` with the images written beside the PDF, as
  Node's default). `preview_pdf(&path, PreviewOptions { cache_root, password, cancel })` is `documentPreviewPdf`; `preview_pages(&pdf, PagesOptions { pages,
  max_width, cache_root, cancel })` is `documentPreviewPages`. `PdfPreview::to_json()` and `PreviewPages::to_json()` are the replies key for key.
- The ext-host worker's `DocumentEngine` (nr-exthost-worker-document-methods, methods/document.rs) is implemented over it: `preview_pdf(PreviewRequest)` ->
  `DocumentPreview::preview_pdf(&file, PreviewOptions { cache_root, password: password.unwrap_or_default(), cancel })`, mapped to `PdfPreview { path, format,
  mtime_ms, size, cached }`; `preview_pages(PagesRequest)` -> `preview_pages(Path::new(&pdf), PagesOptions { pages, max_width, cache_root, cancel })`, mapped to
  `RenderedPages { page_count, pages }` (`PreviewPage` has the same fields). A `PreviewError` becomes `CodedError::new(code, message)` when `error.code()` is
  `Some` (the codes are the `OFFICE_PREVIEW_*` constants of the module, plus `ENOENT`/`EACCES` of a failed stat), `CodedError::failed(message)` otherwise; an
  error with `is_aborted()` is the call's cancellation. `PREVIEW_FORMATS`/`preview_format` of the handler layer is `preview::preview_format`.
  The engine is built inside the `Extension` fn (`|registry| document::register_with(registry, engine)`), as that task's wire says; the route in
  `native_ext_methods` (compose.rs) drops `&& !method.starts_with("document.")` once it is registered.
- The process must call `mixdog_office_pdf::preview::remove_tracked_preview_scratch_sync(proof)` (in a lane job, with the job's write proof) as it ends:
  every scratch directory of a preview (a private copy for Microsoft Office, a decrypted package, an unlocked PDF) holds document content and is removed
  then if a removal did not succeed before (Node did it from a process exit handler, which Rust has no equivalent of). The place is the daemon's / worker's
  shutdown path of whichever task wires the preview; next to `Soffice::process().shutdown(proof)` (nr-office-ooxml-xlsx-charts-soffice.wire).
- Not here (the ext-host track's): the project-entry path guard, the page/width/password parameter checks, `libreOfficeStatus` with its probe cache and
  `installLibreOffice` (winget/brew, `INSTALL_TIMEOUT_MS`) are in methods/document.rs and methods/soffice.rs of mixdog-exthost-worker, already ported.

